  "surprise": "P42 reversed (fork normal(0.02) init instead of the orthogonal override, 186-claude otherwise unchanged) scored 694/671/642 on seeds 0/1/2: mean 669.0 vs 186's 680.33 (668/699/674), -11.3, paired +26/-28/-32, below the registered keep threshold 677.0, so discard. Pretraining was unchanged as predicted: 5,274/5,339/5,392 steps (186: 5,357/5,435/5,355; seed 0's pod started pretraining 5 s later), same ~20 steps/s, val loss within ~0.01 of 186's from 75 s on, held-out greedy 0.965/0.966/0.972 (186: 0.9715/0.9775/0.974). The surprise is the RL start: round-1 targets solved 601/521/277 vs 186's 739/779/711 (sample acc 0.152/0.111/0.089 vs 0.273/0.290/0.231), outside my registered 690-790 on all three seeds. The Lean gate was healthy (nd-only 0); the gap is unparseable samples, e.g. seed 2 had 26,340/48,000 parse failures in round 1 and still 22,101 in round 3 (seed 0 fell to 5,497 by round 2), so its solves went 277/437/578 before a 1,097 round 4. Most of the gap closes by round 4 (1,164/1,159/1,097, mean 1,140, vs 1,172). Reading: same pretraining loss, but the Gaussian-init solution extrapolates worse to >=7-line targets at first, so the orthogonal init is not dead weight under Muon and Peri-LN, though a 3/3 sign on round 1 (p=1/8) and a final within seed noise are suggestive, not proof. Keep the 4 lines.",
